WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.941
Configuring LoRA and the trainer.

2
00:00:02.221 --> 00:00:04.867
Two configuration objects do most of the work.

3
00:00:05.147 --> 00:00:11.312
LoraConfig from PEFT describes the adapter: rank, alpha, dropout, and which modules to wrap.

4
00:00:11.592 --> 00:00:21.619
SFTConfig from TRL extends Transformers’ training arguments with SFT-specific options such as max_length, packing, and the loss masks.

5
00:00:21.899 --> 00:00:26.549
Pass the LoRA config to the trainer as peft_config and it wraps the model for you.

6
00:00:26.829 --> 00:00:30.989
The values in the snippet below are this lesson’s starting point, with reasons.

7
00:00:31.269 --> 00:00:36.261
Rank 16 and alpha 32 (scale 2) on all linear layers, per lesson 8.

8
00:00:36.541 --> 00:00:51.667
A learning rate of 2e-4, higher than TRL’s 2e-5 default for full fine-tuning, because adapters want a higher rate (TRL’s docs suggest around 1e-4; Unsloth’s guide uses 2e-4 as its default).

9
00:00:51.947 --> 00:00:57.152
Two epochs with evaluation every 10 steps, so you can see the validation curve turn.

10
00:00:57.432 --> 00:00:59.032
Precision set explicitly.

11
00:00:59.312 --> 00:01:01.125
Know which defaults you’re accepting.

12
00:01:01.405 --> 00:01:02.643
In TRL 1.

13
00:01:02.923 --> 00:01:19.115
17, SFTConfig turns bf16 on when fp16 isn’t set, turns gradient checkpointing on (less memory, slower steps), logs every 10 steps, truncates to 1,024 tokens, and doesn’t pack examples.

14
00:01:19.395 --> 00:01:27.309
When the model is passed as a string, SFTTrainer loads it in float32 unless you set a dtype in model_init_kwargs.

15
00:01:27.589 --> 00:01:38.576
Colab’s free-tier GPU type varies and isn’t guaranteed; older GPUs don’t support bf16, so detect it and fall back to fp16 mixed precision.

16
00:01:38.856 --> 00:01:44.232
report_to="none" keeps the run off external trackers; losses are still in trainer.

17
00:01:44.512 --> 00:01:45.280
state.

18
00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:46.563
log_history.
